**/*.rs.bk
# lex-code's own session trail (.lex/sessions/*.db) when driven via
# `lex-os exec` from this checkout — a build/run artifact, not source.
# Landed in the tree once already (#86), harmlessly (a trivial local
# smoke test, no secrets), but that was luck, not something to rely on
# for the next person who runs the same command from here.
.lex/
# Cargo.lock IS committed: lex-os ships a binary, so a fresh clone should build
# the exact same dependency versions (incl. the pinned lex-lang/acli git revs).
